WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Dissolve a cobalt two salt in
water, and the solution turns pink.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.590
Add concentrated hydrochloric
acid, and it turns blue.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.550
It's still cobalt, still plus
two, all the way through.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.990
So where does the change
of colour come from?

5
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:21.210
Why is the same cobalt two ion pink in water
but blue in concentrated hydrochloric acid?

6
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.150
In this mission, you'll find out where the
colour of a transition-metal complex comes from,

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.130
and use the colour wheel to link
what you see to the light absorbed.

8
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.690
You'll convert a wavelength
into a frequency,

9
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.150
and find out why some ions
have no colour at all.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: explain why the
cobalt solution changes colour.
